///! net — network primitives + HTTP.
///!
///! Standing up a TCP server or HTTP endpoint should not need
///! third-party packages. This module brings the Go-style stdlib
///! surface: sockets and addresses at the base, a small HTTP layer
///! on top.
///!
///! Deliberately out of scope:
///!
///! - **TLS.** A crypto stack written from scratch is the wrong
///!   call; HTTPS goes through an external library sitting between
///!   `TcpStream` and the HTTP layer. That's the same model Go's
///!   `crypto/tls` follows — it's in the stdlib, but `net/http`
///!   treats it as opaque bytes.
///! - **UDP, Unix sockets.** Easy to add; no caller has needed
///!   them.
///! - **HTTP/2, WebSocket, chunked transfer-encoding, keep-alive.**
///!   The Phase 5 server is connection-per-request; that's enough
///!   for the compiler's dev-server needs and for simple tooling.
///! - **Full URL parsing.** `http::Client` takes a `SocketAddr` and
///!   a path; users that need `https://host:port/path` wrap that
///!   in their own parser for now.
///! - **DNS resolution.** `getaddrinfo` has a linked-list C API
///!   that's annoying to bridge. Users pass IPs directly until a
///!   resolver lands.

namespace std::net;

public module net::ip;
public module net::socket_addr;
public module net::tcp;
public module net::http;
